1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,740
A business brief should become a document a
team can review, not a black box.

2
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:12,700
This is Docentric Copilot: a quotation brief in, a
reviewable DOCX out, with schema, validation and version
history attached.

3
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:19,030
Here is a synthetic package with sample data, parser
diagnostics and a normalized field tree.

4
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:24,355
The schema is typed, so every field the
document can bind has a type and a source.

5
00:00:24,375 --> 00:00:27,548
Nothing is invented from the prompt alone.

6
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:34,170
The brief is the only input: plain language naming the
fields, the totals, the VAT notice and the footer.

7
00:00:34,190 --> 00:00:37,692
The planner turns each requirement into a
typed field.

8
00:00:37,712 --> 00:00:40,508
No model is chosen by hand.

9
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:42,955
Auto does the choosing.

10
00:00:42,975 --> 00:00:46,962
It classifies the brief, recommends a
provider, and then calls it.

11
00:00:46,982 --> 00:00:52,855
The decision card records the recommendation, the model
that ran, whether they matched, and the run identifier.

12
00:00:52,875 --> 00:00:56,484
A recommendation is not a promise; execution
is.

13
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:02,483
The benchmark runs one fixed case set
through every configured provider, twice.

14
00:01:02,503 --> 00:01:08,434
Each row reports valid templates, median
latency and the cost of a valid template.

15
00:01:08,454 --> 00:01:14,657
The numbers are read straight from the report, and the
recommendation follows the report's own policy.

16
00:01:14,677 --> 00:01:18,844
These are observations, not a significance
claim.

17
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:23,023
Download the document and open it.

18
00:01:23,043 --> 00:01:30,075
The preview and the LibreOffice render are independent
views of the same file, and each is labelled for what it
is.

19
00:01:30,095 --> 00:01:36,475
The preview checks content and field binding; the
LibreOffice page checks an independent render.

20
00:01:36,495 --> 00:01:43,548
This is not a Microsoft Word fidelity claim, and not a
claim about Docentric AX compatibility.

21
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:46,118
Here is the defect.

22
00:01:46,138 --> 00:01:53,030
The description column is too narrow, so the text wraps
past the line budget, and the checker flags a text-fit
warning.

23
00:01:53,050 --> 00:02:00,992
Optimize layout applies typed changes to the template: it
rebalances the columns, widens the description and adjusts
the table font.

24
00:02:01,012 --> 00:02:05,580
The panel reruns the checks, and the after
render uses fewer lines.

25
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:09,730
The change is reviewable in the diff, not
hidden in a binary.

26
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:13,956
This is a LibreOffice rendering, not Word
pagination.

27
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:17,885
Every edit creates an immutable version.

28
00:02:17,905 --> 00:02:23,695
Compare versions names each changed field, and Restore
version brings either revision back into the workspace.

29
00:02:23,715 --> 00:02:27,700
The diff and rollback are part of the
deliverable, not an afterthought.

30
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:31,396
A reviewer can see exactly what changed and
undo it.

31
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:36,463
Docentric Copilot is open source on GitHub
under the Apache license.

32
00:02:36,483 --> 00:02:41,908
The demo, the live Auto decision, the benchmark and the
evidence are in the repository.

33
00:02:41,928 --> 00:02:45,564
Docentric AX compatibility: not tested.

